## Design conclusion and evidence boundary

The completed development candidate uses 33 exact stock rows, not a 30-material limit. It preserves the four-part V5 iris nucleus while opening independent root, violet, creamy, dry-wood and late-musk contrasts. The ten module names and seven connections are proposed relationships, not ten observed layers or a measured richness gain.

DHI 2011 remains the target. DHP 2025 is the user's selected structural-method reference: use one iris subject under simultaneous dry/cool and warm/soft pressures, with a recognisable outer contour and late return. It is not an authenticated DHI recipe, a mandatory sandalwood list or evidence that any selected molecule occurs in Dior.

Irotyl is excluded by the user's target and smell preference. No public note list proves a proprietary formula's complete inclusion or absence list. This V6 is a documented successor to V5 after broad research and source-function review; it is not falsely called a newly discovered original formula.

The 2025 primary study distinguishes orris material, commercial alpha-irone, beta-irone and beta-ionone under a small descriptive panel. That supports separate identity and role questions, not universal blending proportions or an assay of these bottles. Beta-irone is not Beta Ionone. [Yamazaki and Miyazaki, 2025](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-08925-z)

Research does not impose a 30-component ceiling: mixture convergence and configural perception depend on selected components, intensities and context. More rows can also mask the target. Distinct roles therefore earn retention through controlled loss tests, not a count score. [Weiss et al., 2012](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3523876/)

## Functional architecture before dosing

The intended subject is root-led cosmetic iris with violet movement, aromatic/fruit glints, cream against grain, warmth beneath powder and a cedar/vetiver return. “Front”, “interior”, “outer” and “rear” describe proposed sensory relationships, not simulated three-dimensional coordinates. Modules overlap over time.

| Module | Proposed relationship | Primary owners | Raw budget (µL) |
|---|---|---|---:|
| L01 — Front glint | Aromatic entry hands restrained green-fruit light to iris. | Lavender EO High Altitude; Linalyl Acetate; Linalool; Coriander Essential Oil | 260 |
| L02 — Iris surface | Violet movement and earthy root remain one subject. | Alpha Ionone; Beta Ionone; Dihydro Beta Ionone | 140 |
| L03 — Living root interior | Rich irregular root remains legible beneath the surface. | Orris Liquid; Alpha Irone; Orivone; Carrot Seed EO | 1680 |
| L04 — Cosmetic body | Powder has a living flower-bearing middle. | Alpha Isomethyl Ionone (Methyl Ionone Pure); Ethylene Brassylate; Benzyl Salicylate | 1000 |
| L05 — Soft interior edge | Cream and dry grain coexist without indiscriminate smoothing. | Ebanol; Sandalore; Delta Decalactone; Hexyl Salicylate | 170 |
| L06 — Fruit-skin connection | Fruit becomes ambrette-like skin warmth without candy. | Verdox; Benzyl Acetate; Ambrettolide | 1030 |
| L07 — Textile and grain | Powder transitions through texture into dry wood. | Cashmeran; Kephalis; Cedarwood oil Virginia; Vetival | 540 |
| L08 — Open outer contour | The receiver recognizes iris-linked character rather than generic strength. | Hedione; Iso E Super; Cedramber | 450 |
| L09 — Warm rear contour | Fabric warmth supports root identity without gourmand takeover. | Tonkarome; Isobutavan | 370 |
| L10 — Skin-fabric return | Iris-root identity recurs in a changed late context. | Vetiver EO (India); Romandolide | 280 |

Benzyl Benzoate owns the separate 80 µL vehicle budget and receives no audible layer credit. The ten primary budgets plus vehicle total 6,000 µL without counting a material twice. Cross-module edges are relationships, not extra material amounts.

| Connection | Owner | Question / test |
|---|---|---|
| T01: L01 → L02 | Linalyl Acetate | Ester handoff omission or alternative at fixed iris nucleus. |
| T02: L01 → L06 | Ambrettolide | Present fruit bridge versus alternative versus omission. |
| T03: L02 → L03 | Alpha Irone with Orris Liquid | Cold-contour and warm-interior 2x2; isolate any root contrast. |
| T04: L04 → L07 | Cashmeran | Texture route versus Kephalis or Osmanthus alternatives; separate intensity. |
| T05: L05 → L07 | Ebanol | Sandalore alternative versus omission at fixed cedar. |
| T06: L04 → L08 | Hedione and Iso E Super, provisional | Receiver identity with outer-contour bridge present versus absent. |
| T07: L07 → L10 | Cedarwood oil Virginia and Vetiver EO (India), with iris family | Late root recognition versus generic wood persistence. |

Open-space purpose: protect iris recognition as intensity falls, rather than equate a strong generic woody/musky cloud with success. Current headspace/evaporation screens do not model turbulent outdoor receiver plumes or individual adaptation. Distance, airflow, substrate, source loading and the receiver must be measured separately. [Almeida et al., 2019](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.iecr.9b01004), [Celani et al., 2014](https://journals.aps.org/prx/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevX.4.041015)

## TARGET / IDEAL — independent mass design

This is an intentionally separate 42-product target design in supplied-product mass ppm, normalized to 1,000,000 with the largest-remainder method from the local relative design parts recorded in JSON. It is a research starting hypothesis, not literature-derived optimal dosing, a Dior analytical formula or a pour instruction. Whole natural and proprietary products are not treated as pure molecules.

The denominator is hypothetical undiluted supplied-product mass, without prepared-stock carriers. For a hypothetical concentrate mass M, a product target mass is M × target ppm / 1,000,000. Constituent ppm would additionally require product assay. No exact raw transfer can be computed without qualified fraction, density or measured delivered mass.

The 33-stock build below is deliberately not a quantitatively equivalent realization of this ideal: unavailable or ambiguous routes are separated, and the user-selected V5 root nucleus remains protected for the first controlled comparison. The ideal is not silently labelled “current inventory”.

