| V5 module | V6 successor modules |
|---|---|
| 1. Aromatic contour | L01 |
| 2. Fruit-to-ambrette relation | L06 |
| 3. Root-rich centre | L03 |
| 4. Cosmetic powder with violet movement | L02, L04 |
| 5. Air around the dense centre | L04, L08 |
| 6. Warm interior and darker grain | L07, L09 |
| 7. Dry wood and root return | L05, L07, L08, L10 |
| 8. Powder-to-skin persistence | L04, L06, L10 |

The six older V4 functions removed in V5 are not erased from the record:

| V4 function not selected in V5 | V6 disposition | Source function retained for testing, not endorsed as fact |
|---|---|---|
| Sandalore | REINTRODUCED_FOR_ISOLATED_TEST | Inherited cedar-to-musk rounding hypothesis. No sandalwood lead; first non-iris omission candidate if no repeatable loss. |
| Romandolide | REINTRODUCED_FOR_ISOLATED_TEST | Outward woody-musk extension; distinct hypothesis from inward fruity Ambrettolide and EB body. |
| Linalool | REINTRODUCED_FOR_ISOLATED_TEST | Small floral continuation of lavender, held fixed; omission tests the aromatic-to-floral edge. |
| Mimosa Absolute | IDEAL-ONLY | Inherited powder irregularity; not a claimed Dior ingredient. Yellow-flower naming or no omission loss disqualifies it. |
| Osmanthus Absolute | IDEAL-ONLY | Inherited fruit-to-violet transition hypothesis; premium 10% stock, not volume grade. Apricot takeover disqualifies it. |
| Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate | IDEAL-ONLY | Prepared dilute fruit flash; separate volatile role from Verdox. Carrier recorded in canonical parent binding, basis unspecified. |

**Formal donor-independence: HOLD / NOT RUN.** This checkout does not contain the DHP protocol's required donor-independence gate API or release integration. The historical extractor also does not recognize V5's prose-only ideal/module headings. The documentary source ledger above is complete for this candidate, but is not a substitute for an executable gate PASS. The theory document is not a recipe donor; an empty recipe signature would be a vacuous comparison. No “DHP-complete”, “equal”, “better” or “deeper” promotion is made.

The protocol nevertheless influenced the actual design: architecture precedes dosing, all source functions are accounted for, the ideal is separate, interfaces have owners, simultaneous cold/warm pressure gets a factorial comparison, and the richer candidate must be compared with omissions before any compression decision.

## Mixing order

<!-- FORMULA_MIXING_PROTOCOL_START -->
This is a NEW-BATCH planning card, not an addition to an existing bottle. Physical compounding, skin use, safety and release remain HOLD.

Before any authorized bench trial, verify every exact bottle label, stock preparation and homogeneity. The inventory binding is not a physical quantity or safety certificate. Record each delivered stock mass by difference; stop if a stock label disagrees. No direct microlitre solid dose is authorized.

Finish each physical basket in the listed order. Within a basket, raw transfer amounts descend; reset the dispenser upward only at a new basket. Use clean compatible dispensing equipment and avoid cross-contamination. There is no chemical-reaction or special premixing claim.

The concentrate table totals 6,000 µL. The only final diluent transfer is 24,000 µL Ethanol 96%, giving a nominal additive total of 30,000 µL. Ethanol and water in the model table are not additional pours. Use ventilated handling appropriate to the supplier SDS; keep flammable solvent away from ignition. No warming, skin application or finished-product release is authorized by this card.

Minimum planned raw transfer is 10 µL. Do not simply divide the row table for a smaller bottle: several transfers would fall below that minimum. A later qualified master-concentrate aliquot route is possible, with its own recorded masses and compatibility check. This document does not assert the mixture was made, matured, stable or pleasant.
<!-- FORMULA_MIXING_PROTOCOL_END -->

